  <div class="about-grid">
    <div class="about-copy">
      <h2>I build the stuff I wish I already had.</h2>
      <p>I’m Jacob. Most projects here start with something on my bench that is annoying, fragile, awkward, or missing entirely.</p>
      <p>I handle the schematic, PCB layout, firmware or software, assembly, testing, and documentation myself. Some ideas stay experiments. A few become products.</p>
      <p>DevGuard 24 came from wanting cheap protection between a bench supply and a prototype. DriverBench came from wanting speaker measurements to be easier to keep, compare, and hand off. The current hardware project is an analog bass-management board.</p>
      <p>The <a href="/labnotes/">Lab Notes</a> are where I keep the useful failures, measurements, and design decisions. The <a href="/products/">products page</a> is only for things that are actually available.</p>

